  "correct": "1",
  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n(5, 32, 7)\n\n(4, 30, 14)\n\n**Logic:** Second no. = [(First no.)² + Third no.]\n\n**(5, 32, 7) **\n\n⇒ [(5)² + 7]\n\n⇒ (25 + 7) = 32\n\n**(4, 30, 14) **\n\n⇒ [(4)2 + 14]\n\n⇒ (16 + 14) = 30\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n**1. (7, 60, 11) **\n\n⇒ [(7)2 + 11]\n\n⇒ (49 + 11) = **60**\n\n2. (6, 65, 13) \n\n⇒ [(6)2 + 13]\n\n⇒ (36 + 13) = 49 ≠ 65\n\n3. (7, 50, 21) \n\n⇒ [(7)2 + 21]\n\n⇒ (49 + 21) = 70 ≠ 50\n\n4. (8, 60, 9) \n\n⇒ [(8)2 + 9]\n\n⇒ (64 + 9) = 73 ≠ 60\n\nHere, **(7, 60, 11)** shows a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (1)\".",
